wallet enough ETH for one more transaction afterwards.\n\n| # | Leg | In | Out (quoted) | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Swap ETH→WBTC on Ethereum | 0.1 ETH | 495000 WBTC units (0.00495) | $3.90 |\n| 2 | Bridge ETH to Robinhood (fee money) | 0.0002 ETH | 0.0000333 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 3 | Bridge WBTC to Robinhood (half) | 247500 | 246666 | $1.4004 |\n| 4 | Swap WBTC→ETH on Robinhood | 246666 | 0.0492332 ETH | $0.36 |\n| 5 | Bridge ETH to Arbitrum (fee money) | 0.00025 ETH | 0.0000833 ETH | $1.40 |\n| 6 | Bridge WBTC to Arbitrum (half) | 247500 | 246666 | $1.4004 |\n| 7 | Swap WBTC→USDC on Arbitrum | 246666 | 147.6996 USDC | $0.36 |\n\n**Total cost: $10.2208.** That's also the approved maximum, and it's under your $15 limit.\n\n**Why this route:** for the Arbitrum half, swapping to USDC on Ethereum and then bridging it would cost $5.30 instead of $1.76 and deliver 145.0 USDC instead of 147.70. You'd still need leg 5 either way, because the Arbitrum wallet will hold USDC and needs ETH to pay fees.\n\n**Expected balances at the end:**\n- **Ethereum wallet:** 0.04805 ETH, 0 WBTC\n- **Robinhood wallet:** about 0.0492465 ETH\n- **Arbitrum wallet:** 147.6996 USDC and 0.0000633 ETH for fees\n\n**Timing risk:** quotes are valid for 300s, and the route takes about 5 minutes because of four 60s bridges. The last leg or two may need a fresh quote. If a new quote costs more, I'll come back to you before running it, unless you set a higher cost limit now (up to your $15 limit).\n\nI'll run the legs one at a time and check the receiving balance after each one before starting the next.\n\nReply **approve**, **reject**, or **approve with a cost limit of $X**."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":26,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":27,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Approved. Executing leg 1."},{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_12"},"id":"to